@page "/"
@inject BrowserStorage Storage
<PageTitle>Verify Wizard</PageTitle>

@* Each paragraph is one source line: a line break inside text survives into the rendered markup as a run of spaces. *@
<p>Pick a starting point. Each flow asks a few questions, then produces a guide, a download and markdown for an AI assistant.</p>

<div class="entry-cards">
    <a class="entry-card" href="new">
        <h2>New to Verify</h2>
        <p>Start from scratch: operating system, IDE, test framework and build server, plus any plugins for the stack.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="entry-card" href="add">
        <h2>Add plugins to an existing project</h2>
        <p>Pick plugins to add. Known interactions with the plugins already in the project are explained, with the configuration they need.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="entry-card" href="add/by-tech">
        <h2>Suggest plugins for my tech stack</h2>
        <p>Describe the libraries in use (EF Core, ASP.NET Core, Serilog, ...) and get a suggested set of plugins to add.</p>
    </a>
</div>

<p class="hint">Every page's url holds the choices made so far, so any point can be bookmarked or shared.</p>
<p class="hint forget">This browser remembers the tech stack, the plugins a project already has, and the maintenance fee declaration, to fill them in next time. <button type="button" class="link-button" @onclick="Forget">@forgetLabel</button></p>

@code {
    string forgetLabel = "Forget them";

    async Task Forget()
    {
        await Storage.ForgetAsync();
        forgetLabel = "Forgotten";
    }
}
